This file is the authoritative record of what is safe to ship. Keep it current
whenever a model is added to `src/bgremover/models.py`.


Models this project can use
---------------------------

BiRefNet  --  DEFAULT, permissive
  Upstream:  https://github.com/ZhengPeng7/BiRefNet
  Weights:   https://huggingface.co/ZhengPeng7/BiRefNet
  Licence:   MIT
  Training:  DIS5K-TR, DIS-TEs, DUTS-TR/TE, HRSOD-TR/TE, UHRSD-TR/TE,
             HRS10K-TR/TE  (open datasets; no portrait data)
  Notes:     The `BiRefNet` general weights are clean for commercial use.
             Some OTHER BiRefNet variants were fine-tuned on private data and
             are marked non-commercial. Read the individual model card, not
             the repo licence, before adding a variant here.

BEN2  --  optional second engine, permissive
  Weights:   https://huggingface.co/PramaLLC/BEN2
  Licence:   MIT   (BEN v1 was Apache-2.0)
  Training:  DIS5K + a 22k proprietary set. Released weights are MIT.

pymatting  --  stages 4 and 5
  Upstream:  https://github.com/pymatting/pymatting
  Licence:   MIT
  Cite:      Germer et al., "Fast Multi-Level Foreground Estimation" (2020)
             https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.14970

CascadePSP  --  optional stage 6 refinement
  Upstream:  https://github.com/hkchengrex/CascadePSP
  Licence:   MIT


Explicitly NOT used
-------------------

BRIA RMBG-2.0 / RMBG-1.4  --  DO NOT ADD
  Licence:   CC BY-NC 4.0. Non-commercial only; commercial use requires a
             paid agreement with BRIA AI.
  Why it matters: RMBG is the default model in several popular wrappers
  (including rembg), so a large number of "free background remover" projects
  are non-compliant the moment they are used commercially. This project must
  stay shippable by anyone, so RMBG is out of scope. Do not add it, and do
  not accept a PR that adds it.

withoutbg open weights  --  not used, but worth reading
  Upstream:  https://github.com/withoutbg/withoutbg
  Licence:   Apache-2.0 for their own layers, PLUS Meta's DINOv3 licence for
             the backbone and Apache-2.0 for Depth Anything V2. Workable, but
             a composite licence rather than a single clean one.


